Tolerate reading newer denotations from stale run contexts

A denotation already brought forward to a newer run can be consulted
through a context captured in an earlier run: TypeMap/LazyRef closures
created before a compilation-suspension re-run are forced afterwards
(capture-checking Setup does this over TASTy-loaded collection traits,
crashing with 'denotation trait SortedSetFactoryDefaults invalid in
run N'). Reading the fresher denotation is safe; re-stamping its
validity backwards would corrupt the newer run, so return it unchanged.

